what about:

```js
const possibleDetectedInsightsClient = getDetectedInsightsClient();

if (!insightsClient && possibleDetectedInsightsClient) {
  insightsClient = possibleDetectedInsightsClient;
}
```

since it explicitly returns false, I don't see the need of wrapping it in a boolean call (&& already does it)

